 The BFD 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Maura Kearns/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 CVC Capital Partners and Japanese buyout firm NSSK have submitted around a $3.2 billion nonbinding takeover bid for Kobayashi Pharmaceutical (Tokyo: 4967).

 Why it's the BFD: Kobayashi was at the center of a 2024 contamination scandal that was tied to kidney failure and deaths.

 The company sold cholesterol-lowering supplements containing red yeast rice, but another fungus was mistakenly introduced during the fermentation process. Kobayashi has denied that any deaths were directly caused by its products, but has made settlement payments and had a founding family member resign as company president. The bottom line: "By going private, the maker of everything from eye drops and skin creams to air fresheners and cotton balls would have a chance to revamp quality controls and deal with rising raw-material costs." — Bloomberg 

 
 
